\title{Reduction in PAC}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{Our idea of reduction should:}

\ul{
\li{\strong{1.} preserve complexity, in that if #{A} reduces to #{B}, and #{B} is efficiently PAC, then so is #{A};}
\li{\strong{2.} allow one to reuse algorithms, in that if #{L} is PAC for #{B} then #{L} can be modified in some standard way to be PAC for #{A}.}
}

\p{In what follows #{X_n = \lbrace 0, 1\rbrace ^n} or #{\mathbb{R}^n}. We also write #{\mathcal{C}_n} for a concept class for #{X_n} and #{\mathcal{C} = \bigcup \mathcal{C}_n} the concept class for #{X = \bigcup X_n}.}

